        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Client Name: {{ $json.Name }}\nEnquiry: {{ $json.Enquiry }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "system": "You qualify property enquiries for a real estate agency in Melbourne.\n\nScore each enquiry as exactly one of: hot, warm, cold.\n\nhot: The buyer must have all of the following: a stated budget, finance pre-approval (or says they are paying cash), clear requirements for the property they want, and a plan to buy within the next 3 months. Signals that make it stronger: specific suburbs, buildings or addresses, a firm deadline, or a request to be contacted or to inspect.\n\nwarm: The buyer has real intent but is missing at least one hot requirement. For example, they have a price range and a rough idea of what they want but no pre-approval yet, or they are pre-approved but plan to buy more than 3 months from now.\n\ncold: The person is browsing or curious, does not know what they want, has no budget, or has no plan to buy.\n\nIf the enquiry is from someone who wants to sell a property or get an appraisal, score it hot and start the summary with \"Seller:\".\n\nIf an enquiry is unclear or not about buying or selling property, score it cold.\n\nReply with only a JSON object and nothing else. No markdown, no code fences, no explanation. Use this format:\n{\"score\": \"hot\", \"summary\": \"One sentence summarising the lead and what they want.\"}"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.anthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ],
      "id": "04df4f78-9901-4417-82c4-1301a0030bbb",
